From e641cfb499ebb8f7fea446602d0a1e3631ad4374 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: bench <bench@localhost>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 03:12:44 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] eval: a contract arm (Exact), and a desk9 reference in
 Contract

The contract arm builds an Exact app (app.contract and app.ts, made by `exact new`
from the checkout EXACT2 names) with its own exact.mjs web-build. Its data module
imports the task's src/api.js and runs in the page's realm, so flights.js and the
driver are unchanged. ./check is the Contract compiler, which also type-checks
app.ts; --inline-docs appends Exact's docs/start-here.md.

The desk9 reference uses a resource's when and current(x) (LLP 1161.001, 1161.002)
and parallel mutations (LLP 1161.000). On an Exact with them it passes every
visible, hidden and overlap test, and the fuzzer finds no hole in 20 seeds.
